content.thinking:
Note: `WeatherViolation` is a record — Jackson needs to deserialize it. Jackson 2.21 handles records natively. Good.

Now the big one: the service. Let me rewrite AirspaceReviewService with the new capabilities. Key pieces:

1. New kinds: WEATHER_MINIMA_CONFIG, FORECAST_UPLOAD, DUTY_ADVANCE, OCCUPATION_CREATE, REVIEW_BATCH.
2. configureMinima(request): validate zone exists (404), windows valid (422), no overlap (422), non-negative (422); increment weather version; replace minima; return WeatherMinimaResult.
3. uploadForecast(request): validate each entry zone exists (404), window valid (422), values >= 0 (422); increment forecast version; insert entries; return ForecastUploadResult.
4. advanceDuty(request): increment duty version; return DutyAdvanceResult.
5. review(request): extended — lock coord_lock (via getGlobalVersionForUpdate), lock route, check versions, read weather versions, compute hits & weather violations, build snapshot, insert review.
6. reviewBatch(request): normalize items (sort by routeId, check duplicates → 422? or 400), hash normalized request; in tx: lock coord_lock, check airspace version, for each route lock & check version, compute conclusions; any forecast missing → 422 whole batch; insert all reviews; return BatchReviewResult sorted by routeId.
7. createOccupation(request): find review (404), check conclusion CLEAR (409), check not stale (409), check no existing occupation for review (409 — actually unique index will catch; check first for clean error), insert occupation with frozen versions.
8. getMinima(zoneId): 404 if zone missing? Or return empty windows. Zone must exist → 404; return current minima + current weatherVersion? The minima's minima_version is the version at which they were configured. Return WeatherMinimaResult(zoneId, minimaVersion of the windows or null if none, windows).
9. getForecast(version): 404 if version doesn't exist; return ForecastView.
10. getReviewDiagnostics(reviewId): 404 if missing; compute per-dimension stale.
11. getOccupation(occupationId): 404; getOccupationsByRoute(routeId): route must exist? Return list (empty ok). I'll 404 if route doesn't exist for consistency with getCurrentReview... Actually getCurrentReview 404s when no review. For occupations history, return empty list if route exists, 404 if route doesn't exist. Hmm, simpler: return empty list regardless? I'll check route exists → 404 ROUTE_NOT_FOUND, else list (possibly empty).

Weather check logic (in review):

```java
// crossed zones = geometric hits among ACTIVE zones
// absolute hits: crossed zones without minima configured
// conditional zones: crossed zones with minima
List<ZonePo> activeZones = airspaceRepo.findActiveZones();
Set<String> hits = new TreeSet<>();
List<WeatherViolation> violations = ...;
Map<String, List<WeatherMinimaPo>> minimaByZone = ...; // for snapshot
Map<String, List<WeatherForecastPo>> forecastsByZone = ...;
for (ZonePo zone : activeZones) {
    if (!Geometry.polylineHitsRectangle(...)) continue;
    List<WeatherMinimaPo> minima = weatherRepo.findMinima(zone.zoneId());
    if (minima.isEmpty()) {
        hits.add(zone.zoneId());
    } else {
        // conditional zone: need forecast
        if (forecastVersion == null) throw 422 FORECAST_MISSING;
        List<WeatherForecastPo> forecasts = weatherRepo.findForecasts(forecastVersion, zone.zoneId());
        for (WeatherMinimaPo m : minima) {
            WeatherForecastPo covering = findCovering(forecasts, m);
            if (covering == null) throw 422 FORECAST_MISSING (with zone+window detail);
            if (covering.visibilityM() < m.minVisibilityM()) violations.add(...);
            if (covering.cloudBaseM() < m.minCloudBaseM()) violations.add(...);
        }
        record minima/forecasts for snapshot
    }
}
conclusion = !hits.isEmpty() ? BLOCKED : (!violations.isEmpty() ? WEATHER_BLOCKED : CLEAR);
```

Also validate: if forecastVersion != null, must exist (forecastVersionExists) → else 422 FORECAST_VERSION_NOT_FOUND? Spec says 预测缺失 → 422. A submitted forecast version that doesn't exist → 422 FORECAST_MISSING too. I'll validate: if forecastVersion != null && !exists → 422.

Hmm wait — but if forecastVersion is submitted and no conditional zones are crossed, do we still require the version to exist? Yes, validate it if provided — it's a result-affecting field frozen in the snapshot. 422 if nonexistent.

STALE determination for current review & occupation & diagnostics:

```java
boolean stale = currentRoute == null || currentRoute.version() != review.routeVersion()
    || globalVersion != review.airspaceVersion()
    || versions.weatherVersion() != review.weatherVersion()
    || versions.dutyVersion() != review.dutyVersion()
    || (review.forecastVersion() != null && versions.forecastVersion() != review.forecastVersion());
```

Wait — forecast staleness: if review didn't involve forecast (null), should a new forecast upload stale it? The review didn't use any forecast; new forecasts don't affect its validity. So only compare when frozen forecastVersion != null. And when frozen != null, stale if current latest != frozen. That's reasonable.

Hmm, but also: what if frozen == null but weather_version same... fine.

Snapshot JSON (weather_snapshot): object with weatherVersion, forecastVersion, dutyVersion, zones: [{zoneId, minima: [...], forecasts: [...]}]. Build with ObjectMapper.

Diagnostics dimensions: ROUTE (frozen routeVersion vs current route version; if route missing → stale, current null), AIRSPACE, WEATHER_MINIMA, FORECAST (frozen may be null → stale=false, current = latest forecast version), DUTY.

Occupation creation:
```java
public MutationResponse createOccupation(OccupationCreateRequest request) {
    return withIdempotency(request.requestId(), KIND_OCCUPATION_CREATE, canonicalHash(request), () -> {
        ReviewPo review = reviewRepo.findReview(request.reviewId());
        if (review == null) throw 404 REVIEW_NOT_FOUND;
        if (!CLEAR) throw 409 OCCUPATION_NOT_CLEAR;
        // lock coord_lock + route row to get consistent current versions
        long globalVersion = airspaceRepo.getGlobalVersionForUpdate();
        RoutePo route = routeRepo.findRouteForUpdate(review.routeId());
        WeatherVersions versions = weatherRepo.getVersions();
        if (isStale(review, route, globalVersion, versions)) throw 409 OCCUPATION_STALE_REVIEW;
        if (weatherRepo.findOccupationByReview(review.reviewId()) != null) throw 409 OCCUPATION_ALREADY_EXISTS;
        String occupationId = "oc_" + UUID.randomUUID();
        OccupationPo po = new OccupationPo(...frozen versions from review...);
        weatherRepo.insertOccupation(po);
        return new MutationResponse(request.requestId(), false, toOccupationResult(po));
    });
}
```

Batch review normalization for hash: sort items by routeId. I'll create a normalized copy: `new BatchReviewRequest(sortedItems, ...)` and hash that. Duplicates routeId → 422? It's a client error; use 400 INVALID_BATCH? Spec: "批量审查任一航线缺预测则整批不创建结果" — 422 for missing forecast. For duplicate routeIds, I'll return 422 too (unprocessable). Hmm, 400 vs 422: validation annotations give 400. Business validation failures here are 422 per spec for weather. Duplicate routeId — I'll use 422 DUPLICATE_ROUTE. Fine.

Also for batch: all routes locked. Lock order: sort by routeId to avoid deadlock. Lock coord_lock once, check airspaceVersion, then for each item (sorted) findRouteForUpdate, check version, compute. Insert reviews. All in one tx.

Review hash for batch must include normalized item set — sorted list. Good.

Now — withIdempotency handles DuplicateKeyException and 409 ApiException by checking dedup. 422 exceptions are rethrown directly (not 409). Good.

One issue: `resolveAfterRace` catches only CONFLICT. 422 passes through — correct.

